The function `iavf_config_rss_reg()` in the diff shows the loops:
  for (i = 0; i <= adapter->rss_key_size / 4; i++)
  for (i = 0; i <= adapter->rss_lut_size / 4; i++)
These use '<=' with the number of DWORDs, causing an off-by-one access beyond allocated memory and register range. The commit only renames macros (e.g., I40E_VFQF_HKEY -> IAVF_VFQF_HKEY) and does not fix the loop condition, so the vulnerability remains.
